sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant OP as Operator
    participant API as Job API
    participant SCH as Scheduler
    participant BUD as Budget
    participant K8S as Kubernetes
    participant M as Machine
    OP->>API: submit selector + reason + ticket
    API->>API: resolve against live inventory
    API-->>OP: dry run — count, blast radius, what it would refuse
    OP->>API: start, echoing the expected count
    Note over API,SCH: count mismatch aborts rather than rebooting a different set
    SCH->>BUD: reserve(service, machine) — atomic
    alt below the floor
        BUD-->>SCH: DENIED — defer to a later wave
    else granted
        SCH->>K8S: cordon, then drain honouring PDBs
        alt drain blocked
            K8S-->>SCH: PDB refuses — mark BLOCKED, uncordon, move on
            Note over SCH,K8S: never force-delete pods to hit a schedule
        else drained
            SCH->>M: reboot(token, deadline)
            M-->>SCH: re-registers with new version
            SCH->>M: health check, then a functional probe
            SCH->>K8S: uncordon
            SCH->>BUD: release — only after verification
        end
    end
    Note over SCH: between waves, re-read fleet health — any failure halts for a human
